---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Compass from '../../components/Compass.astro';
---
<Base current="/en/" lang="en" alt="/">
  <div class="hero">
    <img src="/img/491-img-0577.jpg" alt="L'AgorA's Cherry Island: the cabin at the water's edge, the hammock stretched over the stream, a tent under the spruces, string lights between the trees." width="1400" height="1046" />
    <Compass />
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>L'AgorA</h1>
      <p>Saint-Fortunat, Quebec, 2010–2014. A sanctuary in the forest, built by hand, for people who fit in no box. Treehouses, stages under the spruces, festivals outside the system, mushrooms and permaculture. This is the archive.</p>
      <span class="stamp">Techno-bohemian campground</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="motto">Pirates, pixies and elves. Electro and acoustic trad. Handcraft and earth. A Peter Pan atmosphere, between the Cherry Island, the little island, the yin, and the Neverland, the big stage, the yang.</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">What it was</p>
    <p>On 104 acres at the end of a road in Chaudière-Appalaches, a former pig barn 300 feet long, a barn, a house, a stream, a mountain. From May 2010 on, a handful of "elves" hauled tons of concrete out by hand, then built sleeping lodges, stages, five treehouses, a two-storey tipi, a yurt, an island, a "Neverland", with electricity and Wi-Fi deep into the forest. They hosted festivals from all over Quebec, ceremonies, self-managed camps, solstices, and a great many people who needed to disconnect from the world in order to find themselves again.</p>
    <p>L'AgorA, "formerly Le Donjon, grandeur nature", meant to be a space in nature where "everything is placed at the disposal of the subject, so that they may make of themselves the subject of the work in becoming". A laboratory of being. A village of elves. A micro-society in the making. Four years, some 14,000 hours of work, then the end of the lease, in October 2014.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="facts">
    <div class="fact"><strong>104</strong><span>acres, with a stream, a small lake, a sugar bush and a summit</span></div>
    <div class="fact"><strong>2010–2014</strong><span>four full seasons, from the first shovelful to the last festival</span></div>
    <div class="fact"><strong>5</strong><span>treehouses, plus a 25-foot tipi, a yurt, two stages in the forest</span></div>
    <div class="fact"><strong>14,000</strong><span>hours of work, by Christian's count (already more than 4,000 by spring 2013)</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" href="/en/history/"><img src="/img/303-img-0338.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>The history</h3><p>From the Lune Noire nights in an Old Montreal loft to the last Earthdance of September 2014.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/the-donjon/"><img src="/img/donjon-5505-lounge.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>The Donjon</h3><p>The 400-member private club that came before L'AgorA, from the 5505 to Saint-Fortunat.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/the-place/"><img src="/img/610-plan-agora-festival.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>The place</h3><p>The bunker, the barn, the Cherry Island, the treehouses, the Neverland, the lookout tower.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/yin-yang/"><img src="/img/354-stage-update.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>Yin and Yang</h3><p>The Cherry Island, the little island, and the Neverland, the big stage, face to face.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/mission/"><img src="/img/013-1115924-574389092600219-1707538609-o.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>The mission</h3><p>The founding texts: collective, self-sufficiency, land trust, laboratory of being.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/timeline/"><img src="/img/409-img-0690.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>Timeline</h3><p>Season by season, from what was posted at the time.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/events/"><img src="/img/517-img-0882.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>The events</h3><p>Earthdance, Sundari, Tatanka, Reggae Bash, solstices, ceremonies, self-managed camp.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/photos/"><img src="/img/227-cherry-island.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>Photos</h3><p>More than 200 pictures, from the 2010 worksite to the last summers.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/videos/"><img src="/img/agora-l-evolution-2013-poster.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>Videos</h3><p>"Agora, the evolution", the Earthdance 2010 prayer for peace, the island before the creation.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/voices/"><img src="/img/543-l-agora-bouddha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>The voices</h3><p>What the Agorians wrote, in their own words.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/en/after/"><img src="/img/336-1173631-10152193853423438-1148504371-n.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" /><h3>After</h3><p>The land sold, the trees cut, and the dream still looking for a piece of land.</p></a>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <blockquote>
      <p>"A visit here is a gift for the child, a discovery and an adventure for the young and the grown, and a return to earth for the hearts of many."</p>
      <cite>L'AgorA's Facebook page, spring 2013</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <blockquote>
      <p>"It was a place of ecstasies, of incredible accomplishments, of surprising achievements, of magical visits, of incredible sharing with people so deeply in the true."</p>
      <cite>Christian, co-founder, 2026</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</Base>
